# labwc autostart. One command per line. `&` is required or the compositor
# blocks on it. Changes here need a labwc restart, not --reconfigure.

# --- Desktop portal --------------------------------------------------------
# Start this FIRST. Installed automatically as a labwc dependency, but there is
# no display manager here to start it for you, and without it apps log:
#   "Could not activate remote peer 'org.freedesktop.portal.Desktop'"
# which breaks file choosers, screen sharing and clipboard images.
#
# labwc ships /usr/share/xdg-desktop-portal/labwc-portals.conf, which maps
# XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP=labwc onto the wlr backend.
/usr/libexec/xdg-desktop-portal &

# --- Outputs (monitors) ----------------------------------------------------
# labwc has no output config of its own, unlike niri's `output {}` blocks.
# The layout below mirrors the niri config exactly:
#     HDMI-A-4  1920x1080@120  at 0,0       primary, bottom
#     DP-4      1920x1080@60   at 0,-1080   directly above
#
# Applied with wlr-randr after a short delay so the outputs have finished being
# detected at session start. Note: the flag is --pos, not --position.
#
# Apply by hand at any time:
#     wlr-randr --output DP-4     --mode 1920x1080@60.000000  --pos 0,-1080 --on
#     wlr-randr --output HDMI-A-4 --mode 1920x1080@120.000000 --pos 0,0      --on
# Inspect:
#     wlr-randr
#
# Why this runs TWICE with a 5s initial delay: <core><autoEnableOutputs>
# makes labwc lay out outputs itself during startup, and it overwrote these
# positions at a 2s delay - leaving the monitors side by side instead of
# stacked. Repeating after labwc has settled makes the last write win.
(sleep 5; \
 for i in 1 2; do \
   wlr-randr --output DP-4 --mode 1920x1080@60.000000 --pos 0,-1080 --on; \
   wlr-randr --output HDMI-A-4 --mode 1920x1080@120.000000 --pos 0,0 --on; \
   sleep 2; \
 done) &

# --- Noctalia shell --------------------------------------------------------
# Quickshell-based shell (bar, launcher, notifications).
# niri's config.kdl starts this with `spawn-at-startup "qs" "-c" "noctalia-shell"`.
# Verified working here: noctalia ships a native LabwcService.qml that uses
# labwc's ext-workspace-v1 protocol, and logs "Detected LabWC with PID: ...".
qs -c noctalia-shell &

